# Secrets
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Internal brief — never part of any push (explicit, standing instruction).
flightwiser-brief.md

# Raw / regenerable data
data/raw/
data/processed/
# data/reference/ itself is NOT ignored (unlike data/raw/, data/processed/
# above) — only the large raw downloads within it are. A directory-level
# ignore (`data/reference/`) would have blocked git from ever descending
# into it, making a `!`-negation for a specific file inside it a no-op —
# git's own documented limitation, not a typo. Named individually rather
# than `*.csv`: aircraft_categories.csv lives in this same directory and
# — unlike these two — IS meant to be committed (a small, essential,
# bundled artifact, cf. services/aircraft_category.py), so a blanket *.csv
# pattern would have wrongly excluded it too. The two *_trimmed.parquet
# files (generated from these CSVs) are also meant to be committed:
# pre-processed snapshots bundled with the deploy
# (services/aircraft_database.py, services/airports.py) — production reads
# these instead of fetching ~94 Mo live from a third party as part of
# serving a request (observed failing outright on Render: connection
# timeout to opensky-network.org). Regenerate everything with
# scripts/generate_reference_snapshots.py when the upstream source changes.
data/reference/aircraft_database.csv
data/reference/airports.csv

